From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Trevor Woerner <twoerner@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backend-drm: fall back to the alpha format when the primary
 plane lacks the opaque one

drm_output_pick_format_egl() computes the intersection of the renderer's
EGL-renderable formats and the scanout (primary) plane formats, then
requires the configured/default output format (b->format, typically the
opaque XRGB8888) to be a member of that set. If it is not, output init
fails hard with:

  Error: format XRGB8888 unsupported by EGL GBM or the primary plane
         for output 'DP-1'.
  Failed to init output gl state

Some KMS drivers only advertise the alpha variant (ARGB8888 / AR24) on
the primary plane and expose the opaque XRGB8888 (XR24) only on overlay
planes. When EGL/GBM offers both AR24 and XR24 as window-capable configs
but the primary plane exposes only AR24, the default opaque format is
rejected and the output never comes up.

Only the min_bpc == 0 (default SDR) path has this problem; the HDR /
underlay path (min_bpc != 0) already searches for a compatible format
via find_compatible_format(). Bring the same resilience to the default
path: when the requested opaque format is unavailable, try its matching
alpha format before failing. fallback_format_for() maps an opaque format
to the alpha format whose opaque_substitute is that format (XRGB8888 ->
ARGB8888), so the color depth is preserved. drm_output_render_gl()
already avoids forcing the framebuffer opaque when the chosen format has
an opaque_substitute, so scanning out the alpha format is correct and
the alpha channel is left untouched.

Upstream-Status: Pending
AI-Generated: codex/claude-opus 4.8 (xhigh)
Signed-off-by: Trevor Woerner <twoerner@gmail.com>
---
--- a/libweston/backend-drm/drm-gbm.c
+++ b/libweston/backend-drm/drm-gbm.c
@@ -478,9 +478,44 @@
 		}
 	}
 	if (!found) {
-		weston_log("Error: format %s unsupported by EGL GBM or the primary plane for output '%s'.\n",
-			   b->format->drm_format_name, output->base.name);
-		ret = false;
+		/*
+		 * The configured/default format (typically the opaque
+		 * XRGB8888) is not offered by both the renderer and the
+		 * scanout (primary) plane. Some KMS drivers only advertise the
+		 * alpha variant (e.g. ARGB8888) on the primary plane. Try the
+		 * matching alpha format for the requested one before failing:
+		 * fallback_format_for() maps an opaque format to the alpha
+		 * format whose opaque_substitute is that format (XRGB8888 ->
+		 * ARGB8888), preserving the color depth. drm_output_render_gl()
+		 * already keeps the alpha contents when the chosen format has an
+		 * opaque_substitute, so scanning out the alpha format is
+		 * correct.
+		 */
+		const struct pixel_format_info *fallback =
+			fallback_format_for(b->format);
+
+		if (fallback) {
+			wl_array_for_each(f, &supported_formats) {
+				if ((*f)->format == fallback->format) {
+					found = true;
+					break;
+				}
+			}
+		}
+
+		if (!found) {
+			weston_log("Error: format %s unsupported by EGL GBM or the primary plane for output '%s'.\n",
+				   b->format->drm_format_name, output->base.name);
+			ret = false;
+			goto done;
+		}
+
+		weston_log("Format %s unavailable on the primary plane for output '%s'; "
+			   "falling back to %s.\n",
+			   b->format->drm_format_name, output->base.name,
+			   fallback->drm_format_name);
+
+		output->format = fallback;
 		goto done;
 	}
 
